                <pb facs="0355" n="267" xml:id="pg267"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/2844: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>), <hi
                        rendition="#italic">at Geneva</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-02-02T18:00:00-05:00">February 2, 1933—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>62. Your 90, Feb. 2, 4 p.m. Department did not take up matter with Neutral
                    Commission. However, Department knows from past experience and from recent
                    casual conversations with members of Neutral Commission that they all share its
                    views in the matter. However, Commission as such was not consulted.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
